-- ===== Calcium (calcium) =====
UPDATE api.supplements SET
  quick_overview = 'An essential mineral critical for bone structure and numerous bodily functions. Supplementation is common for those with dietary restrictions or increased needs.',
  extended_overview = 'Calcium stands as the most abundant mineral in the human body, with approximately 99% stored in bones and teeth where it provides structural integrity and serves as a reservoir for maintaining blood calcium levels. Beyond its well-known role in skeletal health, calcium participates in numerous critical physiological processes including muscle contraction, nerve signal transmission, blood clotting, and cellular signaling. The body maintains tight control over blood calcium levels through a complex hormonal system involving parathyroid hormone, calcitonin, and vitamin D, which can mobilize calcium from bones when dietary intake is insufficient. This homeostatic mechanism means that inadequate calcium intake over time can gradually deplete bone mineral density, even while blood calcium levels remain normal. Calcium absorption efficiency varies significantly based on factors including age (declining as we get older), vitamin D status, the form of calcium consumed, and whether it''s taken with food. Understanding these factors helps explain why calcium supplementation strategies often emphasize split dosing and attention to vitamin D status.',
  science_snapshot = 'Clinical research consistently demonstrates calcium''s essential role in bone health, with supplementation shown to slow bone mineral density loss, particularly when combined with adequate vitamin D. Studies suggest benefits are most pronounced in populations with low dietary calcium intake, older adults, and post-menopausal women. Recent research has also examined calcium''s relationship with cardiovascular health, leading to recommendations for obtaining calcium from food sources when possible and not exceeding upper intake limits.',
  key_benefits = ARRAY['Supports bone and teeth health','Essential mineral for many functions','Important during growth periods','Supports muscle function','Plays a role in nerve transmission','Important for blood clotting processes'],
  ideal_for = ARRAY['Those with limited dairy intake','Post-menopausal women','People with increased calcium needs','Vegans and vegetarians','Older adults concerned about bone density','Those with lactose intolerance'],
  timing_tips = ARRAY['Split doses throughout the day for better absorption','Carbonate forms best taken with food','Avoid taking with iron supplements','Take no more than 500-600mg at once for optimal absorption'],
  quality_markers = ARRAY['elemental calcium amount','vitamin D included','third-party tested','USP verified'],
  safety_considerations = ARRAY['Do not exceed upper intake limits (2,500mg/day for most adults)','May interact with certain medications including antibiotics and bisphosphonates','Those with kidney stones should consult healthcare provider before supplementing','Excessive intake may affect absorption of other minerals like iron and zinc'],
  what_to_expect_summary = ARRAY['Calcium supplementation helps meet daily requirements immediately, but bone density changes occur over months to years','Benefits are most measurable in those with previously inadequate intake','Combining with vitamin D significantly enhances calcium utilization','Consistency over time is more important than any single dose for bone health outcomes'],
  typical_dosage_min = 500,
  typical_dosage_max = 1200,
  typical_dosage_unit = 'mg',
  form_notes = '{"citrate":"Well-absorbed, can take with or without food","carbonate":"Higher elemental calcium, best with meals","hydroxyapatite":"Contains additional bone minerals","algae-derived":"Plant-based source option"}'::jsonb,
  what_to_expect = '{"primaryOutcome":{"label":"Bone Support","timeframe":"12-24 weeks","intensity":"Low to Moderate"},"secondaryOutcome":{"label":"Meeting Daily Requirements","timeframe":"Immediate","intensity":"Moderate"}}'::jsonb,
  synergy_notes = 'Calcium works synergistically with vitamin D, which enhances intestinal calcium absorption. Vitamin K2 is increasingly recognized as an important companion nutrient that helps direct calcium to bones rather than soft tissues. Magnesium also plays a supportive role in calcium metabolism.'
WHERE slug = 'calcium';

-- ===== Casein Protein (casein-protein) =====
UPDATE api.supplements SET
  quick_overview = 'A slow-digesting milk protein that provides sustained amino acid release. Popular as a nighttime protein source among those building or maintaining muscle.',
  extended_overview = 'Casein protein represents approximately 80% of the total protein found in cow''s milk, with the remaining 20% being whey protein. What distinguishes casein from other protein sources is its unique behavior in the digestive system—when exposed to stomach acid, casein forms a gel-like structure that dramatically slows its digestion and absorption. This results in a gradual, sustained release of amino acids into the bloodstream over several hours, rather than the rapid spike seen with fast-digesting proteins like whey. This extended amino acid delivery makes casein particularly valuable during periods when the body might otherwise enter a catabolic state, such as during overnight fasting while sleeping. The protein is rich in all essential amino acids, including a robust profile of branched-chain amino acids, and provides substantial amounts of calcium and phosphorus as additional nutritional benefits. Micellar casein, the native form found in milk, is generally considered superior to caseinate forms because it retains its natural structure and provides the slowest digestion rate.',
  science_snapshot = 'Research supports casein''s role in providing sustained aminoacidemia (elevated blood amino acid levels), with studies showing amino acid release continuing for up to 7 hours post-consumption. Clinical trials have demonstrated casein''s effectiveness for muscle protein synthesis during sleep and its potential superiority over whey for anti-catabolic effects during extended fasting periods. Some studies suggest the combination of whey and casein may provide complementary benefits for muscle building.',
  key_benefits = ARRAY['Slow, sustained protein release','High-quality complete protein','Rich in essential amino acids','Supports muscle maintenance','Anti-catabolic properties during fasting','Good source of calcium and phosphorus'],
  ideal_for = ARRAY['Those seeking sustained protein release','Nighttime protein supplementation','People building lean muscle','Those with long periods between meals','Individuals focused on muscle preservation during dieting'],
  timing_tips = ARRAY['Often consumed before bed','Can be used between meals','Pairs well with whey for different timing','Consider 30-60 minutes before sleep for overnight amino acid delivery'],
  quality_markers = ARRAY['micellar casein','low lactose','protein per serving','amino acid profile'],
  safety_considerations = ARRAY['Not suitable for those with milk protein allergies','Those with lactose intolerance should choose low-lactose formulations','Generally well-tolerated but may cause digestive discomfort in sensitive individuals'],
  what_to_expect_summary = ARRAY['The sustained amino acid release begins immediately but the muscle-sparing benefits accumulate over weeks of consistent use','Many users notice improved satiety and reduced nighttime hunger when using casein before bed','Muscle preservation benefits are most noticeable during caloric restriction or intense training phases','The thick, creamy texture makes it popular for puddings and recipes beyond just shakes'],
  typical_dosage_min = 20000,
  typical_dosage_max = 40000,
  typical_dosage_unit = 'mg',
  form_notes = '{"micellar":"Natural form, slowest digesting","hydrolyzed":"Partially broken down, faster absorption","powder":"Mix into shakes, puddings, or recipes"}'::jsonb,
  what_to_expect = '{"primaryOutcome":{"label":"Sustained Amino Acids","timeframe":"1-2 weeks","intensity":"Moderate"},"secondaryOutcome":{"label":"Muscle Preservation","timeframe":"4-8 weeks","intensity":"Moderate"}}'::jsonb,
  synergy_notes = 'Casein pairs exceptionally well with whey protein—whey for rapid post-workout amino acid delivery and casein for sustained overnight release. Some formulations combine both proteins. Casein also complements creatine supplementation for those focused on muscle building.'
WHERE slug = 'casein-protein';

-- ===== Collagen Peptides (collagen-peptides) =====
UPDATE api.supplements SET
  quick_overview = 'Hydrolyzed collagen provides amino acids that support connective tissues throughout the body. Research suggests benefits for skin, joints, and overall structural support.',
  extended_overview = 'Collagen is the most abundant protein in the human body, forming the structural foundation of skin, bones, tendons, ligaments, and cartilage. As we age, natural collagen production declines—typically beginning in our mid-20s and accelerating after 40—leading to visible signs of aging in skin and potential joint discomfort. Collagen peptides, also known as hydrolyzed collagen, are created by breaking down native collagen into smaller, more easily absorbed fragments through enzymatic hydrolysis. This process yields peptides with molecular weights low enough to be absorbed intact through the intestinal wall and distributed throughout the body. Research suggests these peptides may signal fibroblasts (collagen-producing cells) to increase collagen synthesis, potentially helping to counteract age-related decline. Different collagen types serve different functions: Type I is predominant in skin, bones, and tendons; Type II is found primarily in cartilage; Type III supports skin elasticity and is often found alongside Type I. Most supplements contain Type I and III from bovine or marine sources, while Type II is typically sourced from chicken.',
  science_snapshot = 'Clinical research on collagen peptides has shown promising results, particularly for skin health. Multiple randomized controlled trials demonstrate improvements in skin hydration, elasticity, and wrinkle depth after 8-12 weeks of supplementation. Joint health studies show benefits typically emerging after 3-6 months of consistent use, with some research indicating reduced joint pain in athletes and those with osteoarthritis. The bioavailability of hydrolyzed collagen is well-established, with studies showing peptides appearing in blood within hours of consumption.',
  key_benefits = ARRAY['Supports skin elasticity and hydration','Joint and connective tissue support','Provides specific amino acids','Easily digestible protein source','May support nail and hair strength','Supports gut lining integrity'],
  ideal_for = ARRAY['Those seeking skin support','Active individuals with joint concerns','People over 30 seeking structural support','Athletes looking to support tendons and ligaments','Those recovering from soft tissue injuries'],
  timing_tips = ARRAY['Can be taken any time of day','Many add to morning coffee or smoothies','Consistency is key for results','Taking with vitamin C may enhance collagen synthesis'],
  quality_markers = ARRAY['type I/III collagen','hydrolyzed','grass-fed source','low molecular weight','third-party tested for purity'],
  safety_considerations = ARRAY['Generally very well-tolerated with minimal side effects reported','Those with fish or shellfish allergies should avoid marine collagen','Bovine collagen should be avoided by those with beef allergies','Some products may contain added ingredients; check labels if you have sensitivities'],
  what_to_expect_summary = ARRAY['Skin improvements like hydration and reduced fine lines typically become noticeable after 8-12 weeks of daily use','Joint benefits require longer-term supplementation, often 3-6 months for meaningful effects','Some users notice improvements in nail strength and hair texture as secondary benefits','Results are cumulative—stopping supplementation may lead to gradual return to baseline over time'],
  typical_dosage_min = 5000,
  typical_dosage_max = 15000,
  typical_dosage_unit = 'mg',
  form_notes = '{"powder":"Dissolves in hot or cold liquids","capsule":"No taste, convenient dosing","liquid":"Ready to consume, pre-measured","marine":"Fish-derived, potentially better for skin","bovine":"Cattle-derived, rich in Type I and III"}'::jsonb,
  what_to_expect = '{"primaryOutcome":{"label":"Skin Hydration","timeframe":"8-12 weeks","intensity":"Moderate"},"secondaryOutcome":{"label":"Joint Comfort","timeframe":"12-24 weeks","intensity":"Low to Moderate"}}'::jsonb,
  synergy_notes = 'Collagen works synergistically with vitamin C, which is essential for collagen synthesis—many find benefits from taking them together. Hyaluronic acid is another complementary ingredient often combined with collagen for skin hydration. For joint support, collagen can be paired with glucosamine or chondroitin.'
WHERE slug = 'collagen-peptides';

-- ===== Creatine (creatine) =====
UPDATE api.supplements SET
  quick_overview = 'One of the most researched sports supplements available. Creatine monohydrate supports ATP regeneration for high-intensity activities and has emerging cognitive benefits.',
  extended_overview = 'Creatine is a naturally occurring compound found primarily in muscle tissue, where it plays a critical role in rapid energy production during high-intensity, short-duration activities. The body produces creatine from amino acids (arginine, glycine, and methionine) and also obtains it from dietary sources like meat and fish. In muscles, creatine is stored as phosphocreatine, which serves as a readily available phosphate donor to regenerate ATP—the cellular energy currency—during explosive movements like sprinting, jumping, or heavy lifting. Supplementation with creatine monohydrate increases muscle phosphocreatine stores by 20-40%, effectively expanding the body''s capacity for high-intensity work. Beyond athletic performance, creatine has gained attention for potential cognitive benefits, as the brain also relies on phosphocreatine for energy during demanding mental tasks. With over 500 peer-reviewed studies, creatine monohydrate stands as one of the most extensively researched and consistently effective sports supplements available, with an excellent safety profile established over decades of use.',
  science_snapshot = 'Research consistently demonstrates creatine''s effectiveness for increasing strength, power output, and lean muscle mass when combined with resistance training. Meta-analyses show average strength gains of 5-10% beyond training alone. Emerging research supports cognitive benefits, particularly under conditions of sleep deprivation or mental fatigue. Long-term studies confirm safety with no adverse effects on kidney or liver function in healthy individuals. The monohydrate form remains the gold standard, with newer forms showing no superiority despite marketing claims.',
  key_benefits = ARRAY['Supports strength and power output','Well-researched and established','May support cognitive function','Helps with high-intensity exercise','Supports lean muscle mass gains','Excellent safety profile'],
  ideal_for = ARRAY['Strength and power athletes','Those doing high-intensity training','People interested in cognitive support','Older adults seeking to maintain muscle mass','Vegetarians (who have lower baseline creatine stores)'],
  timing_tips = ARRAY['Timing is flexible - consistency matters most','Many take post-workout with carbs','Daily use builds and maintains stores','Loading phase optional but speeds saturation (20g/day for 5-7 days)'],
  quality_markers = ARRAY['Creapure','monohydrate form','no fillers','third-party tested'],
  safety_considerations = ARRAY['Extensive research confirms safety in healthy individuals','Stay well-hydrated when supplementing','Those with pre-existing kidney conditions should consult healthcare provider','No evidence of harm to kidneys or liver in healthy users'],
  what_to_expect_summary = ARRAY['Muscle creatine stores reach saturation within 2-4 weeks of daily supplementation (faster with loading phase)','Strength and power improvements typically become noticeable once stores are saturated','Initial weight gain of 1-3 pounds is common due to increased water retention in muscles—this is normal and indicates the supplement is working','Benefits are maintained with consistent daily use; stopping supplementation leads to gradual return to baseline over 4-6 weeks'],
  typical_dosage_min = 3000,
  typical_dosage_max = 5000,
  typical_dosage_unit = 'mg',
  form_notes = '{"monohydrate":"Gold standard form, most researched","micronized":"Finer particles, mixes better","hcl":"May require smaller doses","powder":"Easy to add to any beverage"}'::jsonb,
  what_to_expect = '{"primaryOutcome":{"label":"Strength Gains","timeframe":"2-4 weeks","intensity":"Moderate to High"},"secondaryOutcome":{"label":"Power Output","timeframe":"4-8 weeks","intensity":"Moderate"}}'::jsonb,
  synergy_notes = 'Creatine pairs well with carbohydrates, which may enhance muscle uptake through insulin-mediated mechanisms. It''s commonly stacked with protein supplements for comprehensive muscle-building support. Beta-alanine is another popular combination for athletes seeking both power and endurance benefits.'
WHERE slug = 'creatine';

-- ===== Curcumin (curcumin) =====
UPDATE api.supplements SET
  quick_overview = 'The primary active compound in turmeric, curcumin has potent properties but requires enhanced formulations for adequate absorption. Look for bioavailability-enhanced versions.',
  extended_overview = 'Curcumin is the principal bioactive compound found in turmeric (Curcuma longa), the golden-yellow spice that has been used for thousands of years in traditional Ayurvedic and Chinese medicine. While turmeric root contains only about 3% curcumin by weight, this compound is responsible for most of the spice''s researched health benefits. Curcumin belongs to a class of compounds called curcuminoids and exhibits remarkable molecular versatility, interacting with numerous cellular targets involved in inflammation, oxidative stress, and cellular signaling. However, curcumin''s major limitation is its poor bioavailability—when consumed alone, it is poorly absorbed, rapidly metabolized, and quickly eliminated from the body. This challenge has driven the development of various enhanced formulations designed to dramatically improve absorption, including combinations with piperine (black pepper extract), phospholipid complexes (phytosomes), micelle formulations, and nanoparticle technologies. Choosing a bioavailability-enhanced form is essential for achieving meaningful blood levels and therapeutic effects.',
  science_snapshot = 'Clinical research on curcumin has demonstrated benefits for joint comfort, with several trials showing improvements comparable to conventional approaches for mild joint discomfort. Studies also support its role in exercise recovery, showing reduced markers of muscle damage and inflammation following intense physical activity. The antioxidant properties of curcumin have been extensively documented in laboratory studies, though translating these to clinical outcomes requires the enhanced formulations that ensure adequate absorption. Research continues to explore applications in cognitive health, cardiovascular support, and metabolic function.',
  key_benefits = ARRAY['Supports healthy inflammatory response','Antioxidant properties','Traditional Ayurvedic ingredient','Joint and mobility support','May support exercise recovery','Supports cellular health'],
  ideal_for = ARRAY['Those seeking natural joint support','People interested in antioxidant support','Those with active lifestyles','Athletes seeking recovery support','Those interested in traditional herbal approaches'],
  timing_tips = ARRAY['Take with meals containing fat','Piperine formulas best away from medications','Split doses may improve utilization','Consistent daily use provides cumulative benefits'],
  quality_markers = ARRAY['95% curcuminoids','bioavailability enhanced','standardized extract','piperine included'],
  safety_considerations = ARRAY['Generally well-tolerated at recommended doses','Piperine-containing formulas may affect medication metabolism—consult healthcare provider if on medications','High doses may cause digestive discomfort in some individuals','Those with gallbladder issues should consult healthcare provider before use'],
  what_to_expect_summary = ARRAY['Joint comfort benefits typically emerge after 4-8 weeks of consistent supplementation with bioavailable forms','Exercise recovery support may be noticed sooner, often within 2-4 weeks','Effects are cumulative—longer-term use tends to provide more noticeable benefits','Choosing an enhanced bioavailability formulation is crucial for experiencing benefits'],
  typical_dosage_min = 500,
  typical_dosage_max = 2000,
  typical_dosage_unit = 'mg',
  form_notes = '{"with piperine":"Black pepper extract enhances absorption ~2000%","phytosome":"Lipid-bound for improved bioavailability","micelle":"Water-soluble formulation","nanoparticle":"Enhanced absorption technology"}'::jsonb,
  what_to_expect = '{"primaryOutcome":{"label":"Joint Comfort","timeframe":"4-8 weeks","intensity":"Moderate"},"secondaryOutcome":{"label":"Recovery Support","timeframe":"2-4 weeks","intensity":"Low to Moderate"}}'::jsonb,
  synergy_notes = 'Curcumin is often combined with other joint-supporting nutrients like glucosamine, chondroitin, or boswellia for comprehensive joint health formulas. Omega-3 fatty acids complement curcumin''s effects on inflammatory balance. Ginger, a botanical relative of turmeric, is sometimes paired with curcumin for synergistic effects.'
